---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { readReader } from '../lib/reader/cookies';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const reader = readReader(Astro.cookies, Astro.url.protocol === 'https:');
---
<BaseLayout title={`About · ${SITE.name}`} description={SITE.description} reader={reader}>
  <article class="page prose-page" style="padding-bottom:48px">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <img class="about-header" src="/media/brand/about-header.png" alt="PulseNSFW brand header" width="1200" height="420" />
    <h1>{SITE.tagline}</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>{SITE.description}</p>
      <p>This is the place you open when you want the new stuff: stars, sites, VR, games, AI, and the toys that go with them. One desk, one search, instead of twelve tabs. It is written for people who watch, not for people who run a studio.</p>
      <p>We publish reviews, ranked lists, guides, and news for people who watch. We do not cover the creator business, and we do not score people. Products and services get a number; a performer gets a sourced profile.</p>
      <h2 id="data">How the data works</h2>
      <p>Stars, sites, apps, toys, and games are one entity collection. An article points at entity slugs instead of copying scores, prices, or pros and cons. Each fact carries a source URL and a checked date. When something changes, the entity record changes and every article that points at it updates.</p>
      <p>Two links are currently tracked: CrushOn and SpicyChat. They are marked in the entity record and on the page. The score is not for sale. See the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.</p>
      <p>Sister sites stay in the footer: <a href="https://companionhub.app">companionhub.app</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
